codemap 9
tour platform-renderer
kind layer
author ai
group render
note The GPU side, the platform crate's Renderer: it replays the ui crate's DrawList (see ui-canvas) with one wgpu pipeline that draws everything the app ever draws as textured, coloured triangles out of a single atlas. The atlas holds every glyph at every pixel size in use, rasterised on demand by fontdue from the bundled fonts (Hack for text, Codicons for icon glyphs, see icons), plus a white patch in the corner that solid fills sample - which is why a rectangle, a line, a disc and a run of text are all the same draw call with the same shader. Positions are whole physical pixels and the sampler is nearest, so text is never scaled or sampled between pixels; a different zoom is a different font size, not a transform. Clipping is a scissor rectangle: every Clip command in the list starts a new batch, so a deeply nested tree is still one vertex buffer and a handful of draw calls. The Renderer is also the Measure the tree lays out with, so layout and drawing agree on every cell size. Nothing it does can fail the frame: a lost surface is reconfigured and the frame skipped, a failed screenshot is reported on stderr.

